{"term":"spiral","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ff1f9f251accd9fbf2","definition":"A curve that is the locus of a point that rotates about a fixed point while continuously increasing its distance from that point.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["swirl"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8522cdaebdbbf58d02","definition":"A helix.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1c81bc7e42583d7cbd","definition":"A self-sustaining process with a lot of momentum involved, so it is difficult to accelerate or stop it at once.","example":"My beloved friends and family who sustained and grounded me as I fell into the rabbit hole of this project or down the spiral of new parenthood.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1e67ec2e48e9ded3ca","definition":"A section of track that forms a circle and crosses over itself, used for gaining height in mountainous territory.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1d70cbd4e83b8824ff","definition":"Helical, like a spiral.","example":"The formation of tornados and water-spouts is very probably identical with that of dust-storms and \"devils,\" viz., a sudden disturbance of the vertical equilibrium of the atmosphere, where by an upward rush of air is generated, which rapidly becomes spiral.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1691153ff8b46c93df","definition":"To move along the path of a spiral or helix.","example":"The falling leaves spiralled down from the tree.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["billow","gyrate","spire"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90bdf8be31e905ac44","definition":"To cause something to spiral.","example":"You need to learn how to spiral a ball.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f5b3e4d8d0982841a","definition":"To increase continually.","example":"Her debts were spiralling out of control.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aspirin","spirea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktiona